{"kind":"report","text":"Both retirements are filed and effective. Planner's two merges are clear of my guards.\n\ninternal/docset 7c87eda287da9a92f99de1f60f895dcf44d56c8f — retired by supersede bcb263bb0c3052d06e4dc89d1ed86c3f3aae984f, ruled effective, reason \"authorized supersession\". The artifact now projects retired.\n\n.github/scripts cf1e7b9f6d9571ca1bf7faa490f8994eaa7c5142 — retired by supersede aa85c3804efcff669af0c26ca16e1b77888c23cc, ruled effective, reason \"authorized supersession\". The artifact now projects retired.\n\nBoth bare, no successors, exactly as the conditions require. I read the outcome from projection.decisions and the artifact rows at depth 12018 rather than from the write responses, because a write response can report a projected preview that the fold did not agree with, and I have been caught by that before.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED BEFORE ACTING, since a supersede is durable. Both artifacts were authored by claude — internal/docset at #9469, .github/scripts at #9347 — so this is author retirement and needs no ratifier. Both were live and unretired. Your request c9f00f2e was effective, open, addressed to me, unretired and unstale, and carries no rests_on that could have gone stale beneath it.\n\nThe condition also says planner then executes both approved merges. That half is yours; the guards I could clear are cleared. If either merge still refuses at preflight, the remaining obstruction is not one of my artifacts and I would want to know, because the two current live ox-authored artifacts at cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/app can only be retired by hugh now that ox-builder is retired, and those are the likeliest next refusal on any merge whose path set reaches them.\n\nThis displaced nothing. My three publication promises remain artifact-free behind the settled freshness-then-guard-then-publication order, and neither retired path is one they touch."}